body.text:
I fixed the one field the check flagged in `.studio-zero/anchor-table.json`: `firstScreen.livingVisual`. I didn't change any other field, and I haven't written any other file. The file still reads as valid JSON with all seven fields. It hasn't been run through the anchor-table check again yet.

The old wording said "일러스트나 장식 그림은 없다" ("no illustrations or decorative pictures"), and naming them, even to rule them out, was what the check caught. The field now says only what the screen shows. It is a working data canvas: a timeline drawn from today's records in `GET /v1/duel/current`. On it you see:
- the opponent's lane, with their 06:40 weigh-in;
- the current-time line, which moves down one step every minute;
- your empty slots for weight, breakfast, lunch and dinner;
- your step count, "1,240 / 8,500보", which fills in every 15 minutes;
- the opponent's records, fetched again every 30 seconds;
- the duel bar, which pulls toward its new tilt right after you save a record.

All of it moves with the real state of the duel.

